      "# rule.always.converge-to-terminal",
      "",
      "work every reviewer to a terminal verdict before a human is pulled. level terminal = every reviewer \`approved\`, \`exhausted\`, \`malfunction\`, or \`constraint\`.",
      "",
      "| the level did | you must |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| approve | continue; next level is live |",
      "| exhaust (earned) | continue; next level runs; answer any blocker it left |",
      "| reject, budget left | fix, or articulate why it holds, re-arrive |",
      "| every level terminal | only now may a human overrule |",
      "",
      "exhaustion unlocks the LEVEL, not the DEBT. the debt is keyed to the reviewer: an exhausted reviewer whose blocker you never answered still holds the stone, and the entrance gate refuses the next round. levers: answer it · budget top-up (if it must re-read) · human overrule.",
      "",
      "exhaustion is earned: budget burned without engagement is a coast. an exhausted level owes a \`.taken.by_self\` record (what you tried each round; what would fix that reviewer).",
    ],
