      "# rule.always.converge-with-reviewers",
      "",
      "a peer review is a conversation, not a verdict. settle it through the absorb loop; escalate only at a real wall.",
      "",
      "| the review is | you must |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| a real defect | fix it, articulate HOW in \`.taken\` |",
      "| a reviewer misfire | hold ground, articulate WHY with cited evidence |",
      "| taste | take their preference unless it regresses a guarantee |",
      "| partly right | fix the valid half, articulate the boundary |",
      "",
      "loop: read each \`.given.by_peer\` → fix or marshal evidence → write \`.taken.by_self\` → \`--as absorbed --that <slug>\` → re-submit. the entrance gate refuses re-submit while a reviewer owes a \`.taken\`; a code fix does not stand in for the articulation.",
      "",
      "persuade with a cited rule, path, or line.",
      "",
      "escalate only for: a foreman-only key · a wisher scope decision · two reviewers that demand opposites.",
      "",
      "there is NO other door out of a blocker: \`…via-a-taken-per-point\` (every point owes a \`.taken\`) · \`rule.forbid.unanswered-exits-from-a-blocker\`.",
