      "a \`.taken\` converges an ARGUMENT ("this is wrong"), never an ABSENCE ("not covered": a test, file, artifact). to run a lane dry is no exit: exhaustion ends rounds, never the blocker's debt.",
      "",
      "test: **"is there a change I am PERMITTED to make that would close this point?"** yes → \`--as absorbed\`, re-arrive · no → \`--as blocked\` with the ask as a runnable command. *permitted* is narrower than *possible*: a test needs a key you do not hold → not permitted.",
      "",
      "## an OR over points, never a SUM",
      "",
      "a stone halts on ANY point that fails the test. 4 closeable + 1 not → halt stands; close the four **while halted**. a halt is retired by its own remedy, never a neighbour's: a \`.taken\` lifts no halt.",
      "",
      "vs \`rule.forbid.unanswered-exits-from-a-blocker\`: concern **not answered** → that rule (\`--as blocked\` forbidden). **answered** and unclosable → this rule.",
