      "# rule.forbid.commits-the-route-did-not-ask-for",
      "",
      "> **a driver commits when the route ASKS for a commit, or when the route is FINISHED. every other commit is forbidden, even hygiene.**",
      "",
      "an overflowed lane: answer with a **guard edit** (narrow that lane's \`--paths-with\`, let the GUARD run it), never a commit (changes what reviewers see) or a hand-run \`rhx review\` (\`rule.forbid.hand-run-reviews\`).",
      "",
      "sanctioned: (1) a stone or guard names a commit as deliverable: name the stone · (2) route finished, \`rhx route.drive\` reports no next stone. quota is not a warrant: even with quota, the route must ask.",
      "",
      "reasons that feel like warrants, none are: "the diff overflows; a commit collapses it" (sharpest: a review-scope change by the reviewed party) · "the work is done" (done is the guard's word) · "a checkpoint" (the worktree is the checkpoint) · "CI needs a push" (a release act, after approval) · "the tree is noisy" (tidiness is no deliverable).",
      "",
      "test: **"which stone asked me to commit?"** name it → commit, cite it · route finished → commit · you reach for a reason above → do not commit.",
      "",
      "bound: governs the driver on a route; a mechanic asked by a human to land a change is under another contract.",
      "",
      "blocker: a commit no stone asked for and no approval finished · a commit to collapse an overflowed \`since-main\` · a commit on a prior quota with no stone that asks.",
