    "file": "driver/briefs/rule.forbid.verbatim-quotes-outside-seeds.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.forbid.verbatim-quotes-outside-seeds",
      "",
      "> a wisher's verbatim words live in ONE artifact: their seed. every other artifact (brief, rule, invariant, yield, fulcrum, \`.reason\`, commit body, PR) states the claim in its own words: no quote, no seed-path citation.",
      "",
      "the ban covers the CITATION. a law carries why it holds, never who spoke it.",
      "",
      "\`\`\`md",
      "👎  > *"only urgent concessions…"* — the wisher (seed S14)",
      "👎  the wisher set the line at shipped harm. ⇒ \`$route/.seeds/…S14…md\`",
      "👍  the line sits at shipped harm: only an \`urgent\` concession earns more budget.",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "| when… | then… |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| you would paste \`> *"…"*\` attributed to the wisher | state the claim, and stop |",
      "| you would soften it to a seed path | same defect, one hop out |",
      "| you write *"the wisher said"* / *"verbatim"* | cut the attribution |",
      "| the quote is "sharper than any restatement" | write the sharper restatement |",
      "| you cannot find the seed | archive it first, then still do not cite it |",
      "",
      "not a violation: the seed's own \`.said\` · a seed cited from within its own route · a published external source · a reviewer concern in a \`.taken\`.",
      "",
      "extant copies: fix forward on contact; no bulk find-and-replace.",
      "",
      "blocker: a wisher utterance reproduced outside its seed · a seed path cited from a brief, rule, invariant, or philosophy · *"the wisher said X"* as a claim's ground · a bulk rewrite.",
    ],
  },
  {
    "file": "driver/briefs/rule.forbid.workarounds.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.forbid.workarounds",
      "",
      "> **never work around a failure. diagnose to root cause and fix there; when the failed tool is one you build, the failure IS the defect report.**",
      "",
      "workaround = a change to an input, declaration, config, or your conduct that quiets a failure while its cause stands.",
      "",
      "bar, a pit of success: correct use meets no friction; any friction is a critical defect, fixed now. wrong state unreachable, or caught once at the cheapest moment with the exact fix printed · soundness by construction, not a list a human syncs · the cure ships with a clamp (red without, green with).",
      "",
      "test: **"did the cause of this failure change, or only my input to it?"** input only → workaround; fix the cause.",
      "",
      "| when… | then… |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| you edit a declaration/glob/config so a refusal stops | why did the tool let that state exist? |",
      "| one cause refuses many times | check sits at the wrong moment; move it |",
      "| contract sound only while a human syncs a list | the contract is the defect |",
      "| you must read a doc to use your own tool right | friction is the defect |",
      "| you write "the tool did its job" about a failure you hit | sharpest cue |",
      "| same failure kind twice | the first fix was a workaround |",
      "",
      "blocker: input/declaration/config patched while the cause stands · a workaround recorded instead of a fix · dogfooder friction left unfixed in its round · repeated refusal from one cause left in place · a contract that needs hand upkeep.",
    ],
  },
]
`;

