      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "test: does this paragraph describe the mechanism, or one time it fired? mechanism → rule · one time → example · no worked case at all → keep the sharpest one.",
      "",
      "blocker: second worked case added to a rule file rather than ejected · occurrences collapsed into one \`example=occurrences.md\`.",
      "nitpick: example with no \`.see also\` pointer from its rule · rule with zero worked cases.",
      "",
      "⇒ \`rule.require.catalog-is-an-index\`",
    ],
  },
  {
    "file": "librarian/briefs/rule.require.summary-at-the-cluster-root.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.require.summary-at-the-cluster-root",
      "",
      "when one subject splits into many subscopes, the summary is \`$subject._.md\` and each subscope is \`$subject.$more.md\`.",
      "",
      "\`._.\` marks the cluster root: it sorts first (\`_\` precedes letters), its path is computable from the subject, and \`*._.md\` globs every root.",
      "",
      "\`\`\`",
      "👍  term=route.stone._.choice._.md          # root, a peer",
      "    term=route.stone._.choice.reason.md",
      "👎  term=stone/_.md                         # a directory where none was needed",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "| when… | then… |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| a subject grows a second file | that is the split; first becomes \`$subject._.md\` |",
      "| you write \`$subject.readme.md\` / \`.overview.md\` | rename; root has a name |",
      "| \`$subject.md\` sits beside \`$subject.$zoom.md\` | bare name reads as a zoom; mark the root |",
      "| you reach for a directory for two files | do not; flat cluster globs better |",
      "",
      "test: given only the subject, can a reader compute the path to its summary? no → root unmarked.",
      "",
      "the summary holds the whole plus an index of parts: what the subject is, the axes, one line per part with what sets it apart, the gaps. it never narrates one part (eject it).",
      "",
      "blocker: split subject with no \`._.md\` root · root named \`.readme.md\` / \`.overview.md\` / bare \`$subject.md\` beside its parts · \`._.md\` root that narrates one part.",
      "nitpick: directory for a cluster of two or three files.",
      "false positive: single file with no parts.",
      "",
      "⇒ \`rule.prefer.decompose-a-subject-via-suffixes\` · \`rule.forbid.itemization-without-coordinates\`",
    ],
  },
]
`;

